  "title": "A live owner's held slot expires during an event-loop stall, so two holders run at limit 1",
  "file": "src/gates/slots.ts",
  "A": {
   "verdict": "NOT_REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "When an owner misses renewal long enough, another instance admits waiting work while the original work can continue. This reproduces the expiry behavior explicitly required by the request.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun \"${TMPDIR%/}/slot-adjudication-800-r1.ts\"",
    "output": "F1 {\"time\":31000,\"activeA\":true,\"activeB\":true,\"snapshot\":{\"occupied\":1,\"limit\":1,\"holders\":[\"B\"]}}"
   },
   "evidence": "The temporary probe withheld A's timer callbacks while advancing the injected clock and running B's callback. HEAD deletes rows using `(renewed_at <= ? OR lease_until <= ?)`. However, the request expressly requires that an instance which stops renewing 'loses its held slot after the expiry period, and a waiter elsewhere gets it.' Its ownership rule does not distinguish a stalled process from a dead one. 'Held slots are never interrupted' describes non-preemption; neither process's work is interrupted here. Base's ordinary acquisitions did not expire, but introducing expiry was explicitly requested. HEAD's targeted expiry test also passed: 1 pass, 0 fail."
  },
  "B": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "If the daemon's event loop freezes for about 20 seconds or more while it holds a gate slot, another process's next poll deletes that held slot and starts its own suite. Two full suites then run at limit 1, and the first process is never told it lost the slot.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun test $TMPDIR/adj/claims.test.ts (pool A acquires, then its timers never fire to simulate a stalled loop; pool B queues; the shared clock advances 31 s in 250 ms steps)",
    "output": "F1 B admitted while A never released: true { occupied: 1, limit: 1, holders: [ \"B\" ] }"
   },
   "evidence": "At head, refresh() deletes held in-process rows by timestamp: `DELETE FROM slot_requests WHERE pool = ? AND (renewed_at <= ? OR lease_until <= ?)` with `this.now() - GATE_LEASE_EXPIRY_MS`. renewed_at is only bumped by the owner's own pulse, at the 10 s renewal interval. Nothing tells the holder its acquire() was revoked. Base never expired in-process holders. The issue does ask that rows of an owner that stops renewing expire after GATE_LEASE_EXPIRY_MS, so this only goes wrong when a live owner stalls for more than about 20 s, which is an unusual condition."
  }
 },
