   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun test $TMPDIR/adj/claims.test.ts (old pool holds the slot and creates a waiting lease, then closes; a new-owner pool heartbeats and releases the lease id)",
    "output": "F2 before restart heartbeat: false\nF2 after restart heartbeat: undefined release: undefined { occupied: 1, limit: 1, holders: [ \"held\" ] }"
   },
   "evidence": "heartbeat(): `if (!row || row.lease_until === null || (row.owner !== this.owner && row.state !== \"held\")) return;` refuses a waiting row owned by the previous boot's owner, both for renewal and for release. The HTTP handler turns undefined into `expired: true`. The row is left in place and refresh() can still admit it until its lease_until runs out (up to 30 s). Held external leases are adopted, but waiting ones are not. The issue's restart requirement names holders, and base forgot waiters on restart anyway, so the cost is a lost queue position plus a phantom slot for at most 30 s."
  },
