    "command": "bun test $TMPDIR/adj/claims.test.ts (one idle pool with db.transaction wrapped to count calls; clock advanced 10 s in 250 ms steps)",
    "output": "F3 transactions in 10s idle: 40"
   },
   "evidence": "The constructor arms `pulse` unconditionally every `Math.min(250, options.pollMs ?? 250)` ms, and each pulse calls refresh(), which runs `this.db.transaction(...).immediate()` (a BEGIN IMMEDIATE write transaction with a DELETE) whether or not any local waiter or owned row exists. attachSlotPools creates two such pools. The issue only asks for polling by waiters. The cost is lock contention and some latency, with no wrong result unless combined with a long stall."
